{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who placed a mouth for man, or who appoints</b> — אם (if). It does not say שם (placed) but ישום (will appoint) — for the future: the lips of falsehood will be silenced on the Day of Judgment, so they find no reply."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The lemma cites the end of the verse where the letters אלם follow ישום; the Ba'al HaTurim reads this as the word אלם (silent), yielding: 'who will appoint [them] silent.' The letters quoted after the lemma appear to be אלם written defectively as א לם, forming the word for 'mute/silent.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:50.791145174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}